Implements three production deployment modules: OSS image storage with graceful degradation, CDN-optimized Nginx config, and enhanced health check endpoints with scheduled CI monitoring.

## Phase 4.2 — Aliyun OSS Image Storage

- **`backend/middleware/ossUpload.js`** — new middleware; activates only when all four `OSS_*` env vars are set, otherwise no-ops (local disk fallback). Includes `safeReadFile()` that resolves and bounds-checks paths against `allowedDir` before reading (prevents path traversal).
- **`backend/routes/upload.js`** — switches multer to `memoryStorage()` when `OSS_ENABLED`; calls `uploadFilesToOss()` directly in route handlers (avoids middleware-as-function anti-pattern). `filename` stored in DB falls back to `originalname` since memoryStorage doesn't generate filenames.
- **`backend/package.json`** — `ali-oss ^6.20.0` added as `optionalDependencies` (install failure won't break non-OSS deployments).

```js
// upload.js — dual-mode storage
const upload = multer({
  storage: OSS_ENABLED ? multer.memoryStorage() : storage,
  fileFilter: imageFilter,
  limits: { fileSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024 },
});

// In route handler — direct utility call, not middleware-as-function
if (OSS_ENABLED) await uploadFilesToOss([req.file], uploadDir);
const url = req.file.ossUrl || ('/uploads/' + req.file.filename);
```

## Phase 4.3 — CDN Acceleration

- **`nginx.conf`** — `worker_connections 2048`, Gzip level 6 with `gzip_vary`, `/uploads/` gets 365d `immutable` cache (UUID filenames make them content-addressed), static assets 30d, API routes `no-store`, SPA HTML `no-cache`. Added Socket.IO WebSocket block (`proxy_read_timeout 86400s`).
- **`docs/CDN_SETUP.md`** — new doc covering Aliyun CDN console setup, OSS+CDN joint acceleration architecture, cache rule table, HTTPS cert options, referer whitelist + URL auth configuration.

## Phase 4.4 — Health Checks + Failover

- **`backend/routes/health.js`** — replaces the trivial inline handler. `GET /api/health` runs `SELECT 1` against Prisma and returns `{status, db, uptime, memory, latency, region}`; returns 503 on DB failure. Adds `/ready` (K8s readiness) and `/live` (K8s liveness) probes.
- **`backend/app.js`** — health route migrated to `app.use('/api/health', require('./routes/health'))` with `/health` alias preserved for backward compat.
- **`.github/workflows/health-check.yml`** — scheduled every 15 min; uses `jq` for JSON parsing; exits 1 if `status === "error"`.
- **`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`** — appended failover strategy section (Railway auto-restart, Swarm rolling updates, Prisma reconnect, replica topology, Aliyun GeoDNS multi-region).

